 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "tsmom000",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Reproducing Moskowitz, Ooi & Pedersen (2012) — *Time Series Momentum*\n",
    "\n",
    "Working through the paper's maths on a single instrument (SPY) to get a feel for what\n",
    "they do. The equations live in `tsmom.py`, each one labelled with its number in the paper.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Three reasons the numbers here will not match the paper**, all worth keeping in view:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **One instrument, not 58.** Their headline Sharpe comes from averaging ~58 weakly\n",
    "   correlated bets. A single equity index cannot reproduce that and should not be\n",
    "   expected to — this is a maths check, not a replication.\n",
    "2. **Five years, not 25.** The Polygon account currently returns ~1,253 daily bars\n",
    "   (2021-07 onward) whatever start date is requested. The paper runs 1985–2009, and\n",
    "   their lag regressions go out to 60 months — which needs more history than exists here.\n",
    "3. **SPY is funded, futures are not.** Futures returns are already excess returns; SPY's\n",
    "   are total returns, so `rf_annual` has to be subtracted to compare like with like.\n",
    "\n",
    "The reference table is a **placeholder with invented numbers** until the real Table 2 is\n",
    "digitised. Everything that touches it says so loudly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "tsmom001",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%load_ext autoreload\n",
    "%autoreload 2\n",
    "\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from massive import RESTClient\n",
    "\n",
    "import plots\n",
    "import tsmom\n",
    "from util import rates\n",
    "\n",
    "API_KEY = \""api_key"\"\n",
    "TICKER = \"SPY\"\n",
    "START, END = \"1993-01-01\", \"2026-07-27\"   # start is aspirational; the account truncates\n",
    "# Risk-free rate. This is NOT a paper input -- MOP trade futures, which are unfunded, so\n",
    "# their returns are already excess. We need it only because SPY is funded. Assuming zero\n",
    "# inflates the SPY TSMOM Sharpe from 0.57 to 0.99, so it is not optional.\n",
    "# DTB3 (3-month bill) is the right rate; the local DGS10 10-year file is the offline\n",
    "# fallback and carries a term-premium bias.\n",
    "RF_SERIES = \"DTB3\"\n",
    "\n",
    "client = RESTClient(api_key=API_KEY)\n",
    "bars = client.get_aggs(TICKER, 1, \"day\", START, END, limit=50000)\n",
    "\n",
    "px = pd.Series(\n",
    "    [b.close for b in bars],\n",
    "    index=pd.to_datetime([b.timestamp for b in bars], unit=\"ms\", utc=True)\n",
    "            .tz_convert(\"America/New_York\").tz_localize(None).normalize(),\n",
    "    name=TICKER,\n",
    ").sort_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "rf_daily = rates.align_daily(rates.risk_free_daily(RF_SERIES), px.index)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"{len(px):,} daily bars   {px.index[0].date()} -> {px.index[-1].date()}\"\n",
    "      f\"   ({(px.index[-1] - px.index[0]).days / 365.25:.1f} years)\")\n",
    "print(f\"asked for {START}; got {px.index[0].date()} -- the account caps history\")\n",
    "print(f\"{RF_SERIES}: mean {rf_daily.mean():.2%}, \"\n",
    "      f\"range {rf_daily.min():.2%} - {rf_daily.max():.2%}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "tsmom002",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Eq. (1) — ex ante volatility\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\sigma_t^2 = 261 \\sum_{i=0}^{\\infty}(1-\\delta)\\delta^i\\,(r_{t-1-i}-\\bar r_t)^2,\n",
    "\\qquad \\frac{\\delta}{1-\\delta} = 60 \\text{ days}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Since the weights sum to one this collapses to $E_w[r^2] - (E_w[r])^2$, so it is two\n",
    "EWMAs rather than an explicit sum. Both run on returns lagged one day, which is what\n",
    "makes $\\sigma_t$ depend only on data through $t-1$ — the paper's no-look-ahead condition.\n",
    "pandas' `com=60` *is* the paper's centre of mass ($\\alpha = 1/61$, $\\delta = 60/61$)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "tsmom003",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "r_d = px.pct_change()\n",
    "sigma_d = tsmom.ex_ante_vol(r_d)\n",
    "\n",
    "# excess returns: month-end price change minus that month's average bill rate\n",
    "rf_m = rates.monthly_rate(rf_daily)\n",
    "monthly = tsmom.to_monthly(px)\n",
    "monthly[\"ret\"] = monthly[\"ret\"] - rf_m.reindex(monthly.index)\n",
    "monthly = monthly.dropna(subset=[\"ret\"])\n",
    "print(monthly.tail(6).to_string())\n",
    "print(f\"\\nex ante annualised vol: median {sigma_d.median():.1%}, \"\n",
    "      f\"range {sigma_d.min():.1%} - {sigma_d.max():.1%}\")\n",
    "print(f\"realised annualised vol (full sample): {r_d.std() * np.sqrt(261):.1%}\")\n",
    "print(f\"months usable: {len(monthly)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(13, 4))\n",
    "ax.plot(sigma_d.index, sigma_d * 100, color=\"#7570b3\", linewidth=1)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"ex ante annualised vol (%)\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(f\"{TICKER}: Eq. (1) ex ante volatility, 60-day centre of mass\")\n",
    "ax.grid(axis=\"y\", linewidth=0.5, alpha=0.3); ax.set_axisbelow(True)\n",
    "for s in (\"top\", \"right\"):\n",
    "    ax.spines[s].set_visible(False)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "tsmom004",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Eq. (2) and (3) — does the past predict the future?\n",
    "\n",
    "$$r^s_t/\\sigma^s_{t-1} = \\alpha + \\beta_h\\, r^s_{t-h}/\\sigma^s_{t-h-1} + \\varepsilon^s_t\n",
    "\\qquad\n",
    "r^s_t/\\sigma^s_{t-1} = \\alpha + \\beta_h\\, \\mathrm{sign}(r^s_{t-h}) + \\varepsilon^s_t$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Pooled panel, t-statistics clustered by month. The paper's result is positive t-stats for\n",
    "lags 1–12 and negative beyond — continuation then reversal.\n",
    "\n",
    "With one instrument each time-cluster holds a single observation, so the clustered\n",
    "covariance degenerates to White/HC. It is implemented generally so adding instruments\n",
    "later changes nothing but the input."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "tsmom005",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "panel = monthly.reset_index().rename(columns={\"index\": \"month\"})\n",
    "panel[\"instrument\"] = TICKER\n",
    "panel[\"month\"] = panel[\"month\"].astype(str)\n",
    "\n",
    "MAX_LAG = min(60, max(2, len(monthly) - 14))     # 60 needs far more history than we have\n",
    "print(f\"running lags 1..{MAX_LAG}  (paper uses 60; {len(monthly)} months available)\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "reg_ret = tsmom.lag_regressions(panel, max_lag=MAX_LAG, spec=\"return\")\n",
    "reg_sgn = tsmom.lag_regressions(panel, max_lag=MAX_LAG, spec=\"sign\")\n",
    "\n",
    "summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"t_eq2\": reg_ret[\"t_stat\"], \"t_eq3\": reg_sgn[\"t_stat\"], \"n\": reg_ret[\"n_obs\"]})\n",
    "print(summary.head(14).round(2).to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "pos_12 = (reg_ret[\"t_stat\"].loc[:12] > 0).sum()\n",
    "print(f\"\\nlags 1-12 with positive t (Eq. 2): {pos_12}/12   \"\n",
    "      f\"[paper: 12/12, nine significant]\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plots.plot_tsmom_tstats(reg_ret, reg_sgn,\n",
    "                        title=f\"{TICKER}: Fig. 1 equivalent, {len(monthly)} months\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "tsmom006",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Eq. (5) — the strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "$$r^{TSMOM,s}_{t,t+1} = \\mathrm{sign}\\!\\left(r^s_{t-12,t}\\right)\\frac{40\\%}{\\sigma^s_t}\\,r^s_{t,t+1}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Long if the trailing 12-month excess return is positive, short if negative, sized inversely\n",
    "to ex ante vol so every period carries the same risk. The 40% target is chosen in the paper\n",
    "to resemble the risk of a single stock; averaged across 58 instruments it lands near 12%\n",
    "portfolio vol. On one instrument there is no diversification, so the realised vol stays\n",
    "near 40%.\n",
    "\n",
    "`long_only` is the paper's own benchmark: the same sizing with `sign` replaced by 1."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "tsmom007",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "strat = tsmom.tsmom_returns(monthly, lookback=12)\n",
    "rows = [tsmom.summarise(strat[\"tsmom\"], \"TSMOM 12m\"),\n",
    "        tsmom.summarise(strat[\"long_only\"], \"always long (same sizing)\"),\n",
    "        tsmom.summarise(monthly[\"ret\"], \"buy & hold, unscaled\")]\n",
    "print(pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index(\"name\").round(3).to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "a = tsmom.alpha_vs_long(strat[\"tsmom\"], strat[\"long_only\"])\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTSMOM regressed on always-long: alpha {a['alpha_ann']:+.2%}/yr \"\n",
    "      f\"(t = {a['alpha_t']:.2f}), beta {a['beta']:.2f}, n = {a['n']}\")\n",
    "print(\"  [paper: positive alpha in 90% of instruments, 26% significant]\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nmonths long: {(strat['signal'] > 0).sum()}, \"\n",
    "      f\"short: {(strat['signal'] < 0).sum()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plots.plot_tsmom_equity(strat[\"tsmom\"], strat[\"long_only\"],\n",
    "                        title=f\"{TICKER}: Eq. (5) TSMOM vs always-long, both vol-scaled\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "tsmom008",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The (look-back, holding) grid — and the placeholder reference\n",
    "\n",
    "The paper's Table 2 reports t-statistics of alphas across look-back $k$ and holding $h$.\n",
    "For $h>1$ it averages the $h$ overlapping portfolios formed over the last $h$ months, so a\n",
    "single monthly series comes out whatever $h$ is.\n",
    "\n",
    "⚠️ **The reference values below are invented.** They reproduce only the qualitative shape\n",
    "the paper reports so the join and diff logic can be exercised. Swap\n",
    "`reference_mop2012_PLACEHOLDER.csv` for the digitised table and drop `PLACEHOLDER` from its\n",
    "`source` column; the warning disappears on its own.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note also that we compare our **Sharpe ratios** against their **alpha t-statistics** —\n",
    "different quantities. That is a stand-in until the real table arrives, not a claim."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "tsmom009",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "grid = tsmom.kh_grid(monthly)\n",
    "print(\"Sharpe ratio by look-back (rows) x holding (cols), months:\")\n",
    "print(grid.round(2).to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "ref = tsmom.load_reference()\n",
    "if ref.attrs[\"is_placeholder\"]:\n",
    "    print(\"\\n\" + \"!\" * 78)\n",
    "    print(\"!! REFERENCE VALUES ARE PLACEHOLDERS - INVENTED, NOT FROM THE PAPER.\")\n",
    "    print(\"!! Any agreement or disagreement below is meaningless until swapped out.\")\n",
    "    print(\"!\" * 78)\n",
    "\n",
    "cmp = tsmom.compare_to_reference(grid, ref)\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + cmp.head(12).round(2).to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print(f\"\\ncells compared: {cmp['reference_value'].notna().sum()} of {len(cmp)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cftc000",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Is the CFTC data the right data?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Partly.** The two families answer different questions, and only one of them can support\n",
    "the paper's measure.\n",
    "\n",
    "| File | Contents | Usable for MOP Section 2.2? |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `cftc_cot_*` | position **levels** + `Open_Interest_All` | **yes**, with a crosswalk |\n",
    "| `cftc_positions_*` | **flows** — buys, sells, net changes | no — no open-interest column |\n",
    "\n",
    "The paper defines\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\text{Net speculator position} = \\frac{\\text{spec long} - \\text{spec short}}{\\text{open interest}}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "which needs levels and a denominator. The `cftc_positions_*` files have neither: they are\n",
    "weekly *changes*, and integrating a change series recovers a level only up to an unknown\n",
    "constant. They remain useful for the Section 6 flow question (do speculators buy after\n",
    "gains?), just not for this ratio.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Where the COT files still differ from the paper.** MOP use the **legacy** report, which\n",
    "splits traders into *commercial* (hedgers) and *non-commercial* (speculators). None of\n",
    "the three downloaded reports carry that split:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `disaggregated` → Prod_Merc, Swap, M_Money, Other_Rept\n",
    "- `financial` (TFF) → Dealer, Asset_Mgr, Lev_Money, Other_Rept\n",
    "- `index_trader` → `Comm_*_NoCIT` / `NComm_*_NoCIT` — legacy-shaped, but with index\n",
    "  traders removed, ~19 agricultural contracts only, ending 2022\n",
    "\n",
    "So `util/cftc.py` applies an explicit crosswalk. It is a judgement call, not an identity —\n",
    "**swap dealers are the contentious bucket**: they hedge index exposure, so they sit on the\n",
    "commercial side even though the flow behind them is speculative. `net_speculator_position()`\n",
    "takes `spec=` / `hedge=` overrides so that assumption can be tested rather than inherited.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Two coverage gaps against the paper:** these start in 2006, whereas MOP run 1965–2009 —\n",
    "so the overlap is four years at the very end of their sample. For the exact legacy series,\n",
    "`deacot<YEAR>.zip` (1986 onward) is a separate download."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cftc001",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, \".\")\n",
    "from research import ROLL, CUM\n",
    "from util import cftc\n",
    "\n",
    "# The disaggregated file is 162 MB, so always pass `contracts=` to filter on read.\n",
    "cot = cftc.load_cot(\"financial\", contracts=\"E-MINI S&P 500\",\n",
    "                    extra_columns=[\"CFTC_Contract_Market_Code\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Select by CONTRACT CODE, not name: the CFTC renames contracts mid-series. The E-mini\n",
    "# S&P 500 trades under code 13874A throughout, but appears as \"E-MINI S&P 500 STOCK\n",
    "# INDEX\" until 2022-02 and \"E-MINI S&P 500\" after -- filtering on either name silently\n",
    "# truncates the history.\n",
    "print(cot.groupby([\"CFTC_Contract_Market_Code\", cftc.NAME_COL])\n",
    "         .agg(weeks=(\"report_date\", \"size\"), first=(\"report_date\", \"min\"),\n",
    "              last=(\"report_date\", \"max\")).to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "CONTRACT_CODE = \"13874A\"          # E-mini S&P 500; SPY tracks the same index\n",
    "es = cftc.net_speculator_position(\n",
    "    cot[cot[\"CFTC_Contract_Market_Code\"] == CONTRACT_CODE], \"financial\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\ncode {CONTRACT_CODE}: {len(es):,} weekly rows   \"\n",
    "      f\"{es['report_date'].min().date()} -> {es['report_date'].max().date()}\")\n",
    "print(es[[\"report_date\", \"Open_Interest_All\", \"spec_long\", \"spec_short\",\n",
    "          \"net_spec_position\", \"net_hedge_position\"]].tail(5).to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print(f\"\\nnet_spec_position  mean {es['net_spec_position'].mean():+.3f}  \"\n",
    "      f\"min {es['net_spec_position'].min():+.3f}  \"\n",
    "      f\"max {es['net_spec_position'].max():+.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cftc002",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 5–6: do speculators trade *with* the trend?\n",
    "\n",
    "The paper's finding is that speculators are trend followers — net speculator positions\n",
    "rise after positive returns and fall after negative ones — and that hedgers take the\n",
    "other side, so speculators profit at their expense.\n",
    "\n",
    "MOP flag the **S&P 500 as the one exception**: it is the single contract where net\n",
    "speculator positions carry the opposite sign, though close to zero. That makes it an\n",
    "awkward instrument to test the general claim on, and a pointed one to check the\n",
    "exception on.\n",
    "\n",
    "Below is the regression in the paper's spirit, on what we have:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\Delta\\,\\text{Net spec position}_t = \\alpha + \\beta \\cdot r_{t-12,t} + \\varepsilon_t$$\n",
    "\n",
    "⚠️ Two limits make this indicative only. SPY history from Polygon starts 2021, so the\n",
    "overlap with the COT series is ~5 years of monthly observations. And a single contract\n",
    "gives no cross-sectional support — the paper pools 58."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cftc003",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# COT is weekly; take the last observation in each month so it joins to `monthly`.\n",
    "cot_m = cftc.to_monthly(es, value_cols=[\"net_spec_position\", \"net_hedge_position\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "joined = monthly.join(cot_m, how=\"inner\")\n",
    "joined[\"d_net_spec\"] = joined[\"net_spec_position\"].diff()\n",
    "joined[\"trail_12m\"] = tsmom.trailing_return(joined[\"ret\"], 12)\n",
    "joined[\"trail_1m\"] = joined[\"ret\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"overlap: {len(joined)} months   \"\n",
    "      f\"{joined.index.min()} -> {joined.index.max()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "for lookback in (\"trail_1m\", \"trail_12m\"):\n",
    "    d = joined[[\"d_net_spec\", lookback]].dropna()\n",
    "    if len(d) < 6:\n",
    "        print(f\"{lookback}: only {len(d)} usable months, skipping\")\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    X = np.column_stack([np.ones(len(d)), d[lookback].to_numpy()])\n",
    "    beta, se, t, n, _ = tsmom._ols_clustered(d[\"d_net_spec\"], X, d.index)\n",
    "    print(f\"d(net spec) on {lookback:<10} beta {beta[1]:+.4f}  t {t[1]:+.2f}  n {n}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\n  [paper: speculators trend-follow, so beta > 0 -- except in the S&P 500,\")\n",
    "print(\"   where they report the sign is reversed and close to zero]\")\n",
    "\n",
    "corr = joined[[\"net_spec_position\", \"net_hedge_position\"]].corr().iloc[0, 1]\n",
    "print(f\"\\ncorr(net spec, net hedge) = {corr:+.3f}\")\n",
    "print(\"  [paper: spec and hedge are near-mirror images, so this should be strongly\")\n",
    "print(\"   negative. Anything else means the crosswalk is mixing the two sides.]\")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(13, 4))\n",
    "x = joined.index.to_timestamp()\n",
    "ax.plot(x, joined[\"net_spec_position\"], color=ROLL, lw=1.6, label=\"net speculator position\")\n",
    "ax.plot(x, joined[\"net_hedge_position\"], color=CUM, lw=1.6, label=\"net hedger position\")\n",
    "ax.axhline(0, color=\"#999999\", lw=0.8)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"share of open interest\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(f\"{\"E-mini S&P 500\"}: positions as a share of open interest\")\n",
    "ax.legend(frameon=False)\n",
    "ax.grid(axis=\"y\", lw=0.5, alpha=0.3); ax.set_axisbelow(True)\n",
    "for s in (\"top\", \"right\"):\n",
    "    ax.spines[s].set_visible(False)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "tsmom010",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Where this leaves us\n",
    "\n",
    "The maths runs end to end and every equation is in `tsmom.py` next to its number in the\n",
    "paper. What is *not* yet a replication:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Needed | Have | Blocker |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| 1985–2009 | 2021–2026 | Polygon history cap |\n",
    "| 58 futures across 4 asset classes | 1 equity ETF | data + instrument coverage |\n",
    "| Excess returns | total returns | no risk-free series wired in (`RF_ANNUAL = 0`) |\n",
    "| Table 2 alpha t-stats | placeholder | digitising in progress |\n",
    "| MSCI World / Barclays Agg / GSCI / FF factors | none | needed for Eq. (4) alphas |\n",
    "\n",
    "The cheapest real step once the account is upgraded is **breadth, not history** — a dozen\n",
    "liquid ETFs spanning equities, bonds, commodities and FX gets far closer to the paper's\n",
    "structure than a longer run of SPY alone, and it is the same argument `theory.md` makes\n",
    "about statistical power."
   ]
  }
